# The archives this repository has been pinned to, in the format `sha256sum` writes and reads, so
# that `sha256sum -c keepass.sha256` checks them too. More than one line is deliberate: going back
# to an earlier pin then needs no network and no trust decision.
#
# A new line is added by pinning a version in `keepass.version`, running `.\build.ps1 -Task KeePass`
# once to be told what arrived, checking by hand that the `KeePass.exe` in the archive it kept
# carries a valid Authenticode signature of KeePass's author, and putting that here if it is what
# was meant. A line here is the whole of what any build checks of KeePass from then on.
3952354DB9B117E906F7CD4F9F5591065B95186472370DA47F46F3E246FEA864  KeePass-2.61.1.zip
